## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to formalize a cost-benefit for a privacy-preserving on-device biometric feature, balancing security, UX latency, and regulatory constraints.

## Key Concepts

- On-device ML footprint and energy budgeting
- Privacy-by-design and regulatory alignment (DP, PCI-DSS)
- Drift detection, calibration, and validation cost modeling
- OTA bandwidth planning and rollout strategy

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode sketch for enrollment and verification flow
function enroll(userAudio) {
  const embedding = model.extract(userAudio);
  secureStore.save(hash(embedding));
}
function verify(inputAudio) {
  const embedding = model.extract(inputAudio);
  return compare(hash(embedding), secureStore.getAllHashes());
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test spoofing resistance and liveness?
- What telemetry would you collect without compromising privacy?
- How would you handle template drift if a user changes voice over time?

## Why This Is Asked
CBA for an offline-first backup feature requires tangible cost knobs and measurable outcomes beyond accuracy or latency; beginner-friendly but demonstrates ability to quantify trade-offs and plan rollout.

## Key Concepts
- Energy budgeting per photo and dedup impact
- Data minimization and privacy/compliance
- Rollout, offline fallback, drift/maintenance, break-even

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo energy check before upload
function shouldUpload(photoSizeMB, currentEnergyJ, thresholdJ){
  const dedupFactor = 1.5;
  const energyPerMB = 0.25;
  const energy = photoSizeMB * energyPerMB * dedupFactor;
  return (currentEnergyJ - energy) > thresholdJ;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure de-dup effectiveness in production?
- What metrics trigger rollback during rollout?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess the ability to translate usage into a cost-benefit framework for a privacy-preserving, offline-first sync feature, including storage, energy, and cloud costs.

## Key Concepts

- Data sizing and retention policies
- On-device energy and encryption overhead
- Cloud storage/egress pricing and scaling
- Privacy/compliance considerations and opt-in flows
- Go/no-go criteria and break-even analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
function estimateAnnualCost({clipsPerDay, bytesPerClip, retentionDaysCloud, users, costPerGB}) {
  const perUserMB = clipsPerDay * bytesPerClip * 365 / (1024 * 1024);
  const cloudGB = clipsPerDay * bytesPerClip * retentionDaysCloud * 365 / (1024 * 1024 * 1024);
  const monthlyCost = (cloudGB * costPerGB) / 12;
  const totalMonthly = monthlyCost * users;
  return { perUserMB, cloudGB, totalMonthly };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust the CBA for user growth and volatility in clip frequency?
- What privacy/consent controls would you expose, and how would they impact costs and ROI?

