## Why This Is Asked
New angle on CBA: gating cross‑app features via an on‑device policy engine, balancing UX, energy, and safety with cloud updates.

## Key Concepts
- On‑device policy engines and gating rules
- Resource awareness (battery, thermal, memory)
- Telemetry footprint and privacy compliance
- Rollout strategy and break‑even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldRunFeature(state, policy) {
  if (state.battery < 20) return false;
  if (state.temperature > 45) return false;
  if (state.freeMemory < 200) return false;
  return policy.allowsFeature;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify risk of safety incidents vs false positives?
- What metrics would drive policy update cadence and rollouts across device generations?

## Why This Is Asked
This question explores a privacy-preserving on-device machine learning use case with real-world constraints including energy efficiency, latency requirements, data minimization principles, and regulatory compliance. It emphasizes the importance of measurable go/no-go criteria and a concrete break-even timeline for implementation decisions.

## Key Concepts
- On-device machine learning models (autoencoder/isolation forest)
- Energy and performance budgeting for background tasks
- Data minimization and privacy impact assessments
- Go/No-Go criteria and break-even horizon analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function detectAnomaly(readings, threshold){
  const mean = readings.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/readings.length;
  const variance = readings.reduce((a,b)=>a+Math.pow(b-mean,2),0)/readings.length;
  return Math.abs(readings[readings.length-1] - mean) > threshold * Math.sqrt(variance);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of data footprint, latency budgets, and privacy controls for real-time collaboration features; also assesses ability to translate qualitative benefits into concrete, time-bound financial metrics.

## Key Concepts

- Delta encoding for presence data (cursor positions, editors yes/no)
- On-device aggregation to minimize network traffic
- Privacy/compliance considerations (opt-in, data minimization, retention)
- Latency budgets for real-time UI updates
- Cost modeling (server/storage, bandwidth) and break-even criteria

